4 Architecture
**************

Perlthon has a layered architecture:

     Python <-> perlthon (Python) <-> _core (Rust/PyO3) <-> perl_glue.c <-> libperl

‘perlthon/’
     Pure Python API layer providing ‘use’, ‘eval’, ‘call’, and
     ‘PerlModule’.

‘src/lib.rs’
     Rust FFI bindings to the C glue, plus PyO3 wrapper classes exposing
     ‘PerlInterpreter’ to Python.

‘csrc/perl_glue.c’
     Thin C wrapper around Perl's macro-heavy embedding API. Handles
     interpreter lifecycle, ‘eval_pv’, ‘call_pv’, ‘call_method’, SV type
     introspection, and value marshalling.

‘build.rs’
     Build script that discovers Perl via ‘ExtUtils::Embed’, compiles
     the C glue, and handles ‘libperl.so’ discovery.


